    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d188">

                <pb facs="0250" n="240" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg240"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/5–1848: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-05-18T16:00:00+09:00">May 18, 1948—4 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 18—9:41 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>892. Personal for Butterworth. Heartily approve suggested statement by Secretary
                    on occasion inauguration President and Vice President May 20, Deptel 735 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">734</hi>], May 14, 7 p. m.<anchor n="48"
                        xml:id="d188-f1"/> Such statement will greatly strengthen my hands in
                    discussion I plan to have with Gimo as soon as possible, following inauguration,
                    in which I hope to stress my belief that reform movement is irresistible and
                    that unless he goes along with it, he will inevitably fail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d188-f1" n="48" xml:id="d188-f1-content">
                <p>The statement was released to the press on May 20; see Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, May 30, 1948, p. 713.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
